{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1189153-can-mages-yank-something-from-the-past-or-future","id":1189153,"title":"Can mages \"yank\" something from the past or future?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-24T01:38:44-08:00","id":1189153,"title":"Can mages \"yank\" something from the past or future?","content":"Well since Mages tend to do what ever if they can put their will to it, can they actually summon or teleport something out of it's timeline and into his, or something like that, by accident or intentionally.If they can't, can any other race pull it off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:17:16-08:00","id":1189157,"title":"","content":"It *is* possible, but without proper preparation the mage will probably fail. With enough dots in Time, Correspondence and Matter (or Life, if you want to summon a living entity), you could pull this off.<br /> <br /> As a ST, I'd rule Time 5 to be absolutely necessary to &quot;grab through time&quot;. It's the only Sphere level to actually describe something even close to this idea. Also, you'd need at least Matter/Life 4 to grab said object or creature. A ST could rule that you'd need at least as many successes as the creatures WIllpower or something. If you know you're grabbing an item out of the past/future, that's not at the same exact location than you are, Correspondence 5 will be necessary, as you need to grab through Time *and* Space to accomplish this feat.<br /> This feat of Time Magic would always be vulgar. It might be at least an Impressive Feat, adding to the difficulty of the roll. Also, when affecting the past, the base difficulty is always at least 9.<br /> <br /> There could also be some fun consequences. Like, grabbing something from the future and later realizing, it's a really important item that is now lost to time.<br /> <br /> As a non-intentionally feat, I'd rule this nearly impossible. A mage with this much power and mastery of his art is unlikely to unintentionally cast magic at all (save for someone with Wild Magic). Also, the amount of successes you'd need to do this would be way above your Arete Dice Pool and the difficulty is through the roof, it should be a ritual no matter what.<br /> Now, for an Awakening effect, this might actually work. As a ST I rule the highest effect of an Awakening to be equal to the Avatar-rating of the mage. So, an Avatar 5 Mage might find some kind of futuristic weapon when grabbing something to defend himself against those weird MiB-type guys attacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:25:23-08:00","id":1189159,"title":"","content":"Well that means some certain creature could be taken from the past and be brought into the future, tho probablly changing the time space continium thingymcbob, but the creature taken from the past/Future is unharmed or it has any side effects?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:36:17-08:00","id":1189169,"title":"","content":"A normal person/animal might be a bit confused, when yanked through time (and space, probably). Also, if it's a sleeper you're summoning, he/she's a witness, making the spell that much harder.<br /> Any bygone/future HIT-Mark Model/supernatural creature might be able to resist the magic, needs his willpower score to be equaled in successes or whatever you think works best in your game.<br /> Also, at least in conventional reality zones, bygones, futuristic equipment or enhancements, antique machines or whatever might be subject to Disbelief and permanent Paradox. Everything that's not part of the timestream might be rejected at one point or corroded by time.<br /> A person summoned from the medieval times could find himself aging rapidly while a futuristic weapon would cease functioning without any spare parts to be available in your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T12:23:11-08:00","id":1189278,"title":"","content":"So, it would probablly pass like 5 to 10 years before that creature is caught up in time and aged into ash and dust?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T01:16:02-08:00","id":1189365,"title":"","content":"That's entirely on the Storyteller. If a ST decides there are no consequences, then there are no consequences and Plato, although he should have died ages ago, may life happily in the 21st century because your mage brought him here.<br /> For balancing reasons and because it's stupid otherwise, I'd rule that time would try to keep up with poor Plato in a very fast and brutal manner. Way faster than for, let's say, Marylin Monroe who's not dead for that long. Plato may die in a number of days, while Marylin might survive a few years until time takes her away. A bronze age tool may wither in a few short hours, while the new PS5 you transported to 2018 may work for a couple of months, maybe even long enough for the new console generation to be released, freeing it from the time-paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T20:08:08-08:00","id":1189518,"title":"","content":"If you could transport something through space time, I assume that the magic to stop it degrading would be easier, even if it needs to be cast often, or sustained in some way.<br /> Look at time travel movies and series on the paradox of changing things, and work try to work out a non-paradox inducing way to do it (Eg creating Marilyn's Body double, make it look like it's overdosed and swapping them both out at the same instant on the night of her historic death) so that history is not affected by your effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T02:17:50-08:00","id":1189560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1189153-can-mages-yank-something-from-the-past-or-future?p=1189518#post1189518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could transport something through space time, I assume that the magic to stop it degrading would be easier, even if it needs to be cast often, or sustained in some way.<br /> Look at time travel movies and series on the paradox of changing things, and work try to work out a non-paradox inducing way to do it (Eg creating Marilyn's Body double, make it look like it's overdosed and swapping them both out at the same instant on the night of her historic death) so that history is not affected by your effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, that's a way to minimize paradox. I did'nt think about how to make this less paradoxy but how it could actually be possible in the first place.<br /> However, poor Marylin would still be very disoriented and she would definitely not belong into 2018. That's why she would deteriorate. However, your approach might be a way to make this spell more reliable, because doing something vulgar in the past pretty much loads a hell of a lot of paradox on you that will work on reversing your effect. (Of course you can still try to make Marylin immune to time, which would end the deterioration but still leaves permadox to be handled.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T15:50:42-08:00","id":1189716,"title":"","content":"I look at the Bill and Ted movies as excellent uses of time travel (First more than second) because of the incidental bits; not when they're changing time on purpose, but trying to deal with good in the present and they remind themselves to come back to help current selves, by dropping things on pursuers etc.<br /> Because it has always happened that way, there is no paradox to deal with. <br /> In the case of Marilyn (our example today) you make it that her body was always replaced and everything in history will still present in the exact same way. No Paradox.<br /> You replace Elvis with an impersonator (to match conspiracy theories) Just before the Fat Elvis stage and then that saved Elvis stupidly is seen around the place occasionally (Elvis sightings) all as history has shown anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T02:19:17-08:00","id":1189810,"title":"","content":"Yes, there are a lot of theories about Elvis but &quot;common sense&quot; dictates he must be dead and everything else is bullshit. Now, if you as a ST decide the conspiracy theories around Elvis have more weight in Consensus Reality than &quot;common sense&quot; (which, in some Incarnations of the World of Darkness may very well be true), then your plan may work flawlessly. If, however, the Consensus Reality is dictated by &quot;common sense&quot; and conspiracy theorists are (mostly) a bunch of dreamers and crazys, then the rules of time travel as explained in HDYDT Paradox or maybe Old Man Wrinkle (or whoever takes his place) might wreck your plan in a matter of seconds.<br /> <br /> As a ST I'd say, you may very well try if you have the spheres. It wouldn't be impossible just very tricky and your approach is quite creative. Every storyteller has a different opinion, however, and that's why it's hard to really answer the OPs question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T18:00:01-08:00","id":1190079,"title":"","content":"If &quot;There was a faulty gas main nearby&quot; Can alleviate paradox for a fireball, then I figure the conspiracy theorists &quot;could&quot; be right as pretty viable.<br /> By keeping history the same for all viewers of the events, there is very little &quot;Paradox&quot; created.<br /> <br /> Sort of like with Quantum physics. Both options could be true at the same time (Particle of light versus wave length) it is only once examined that we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T19:46:31-08:00","id":1192499,"title":"","content":"To my way of thinking, the somewhat fluid nature of consensual reality doesn't lend itself to the idea of the past being immutable or the universe reacting to alterations to it as some kind of \u00fcber-paradox that messes up things in vastly wider scope than alterations using the other spheres. What if the past is changing all the time, and people just don't notice because their memories change to match?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:01:18-08:00","id":1192523,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3505_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3505\" data-vbnamecard=\"3505\">Matt the Bruins fan</a> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/xaq21T\" target=\"_blank\">https://goo.gl/images/xaq21T</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:41:04-08:00","id":1192537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1189153-can-mages-yank-something-from-the-past-or-future?p=1192499#post1192499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the past is changing all the time, and people just don't notice because their memories change to match?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or what if the past changes because people share a wrong memory...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:35:08-08:00","id":1193195,"title":"","content":"Or what if you actually want to balance the effects your players mages cast to not destroy your game? My thoughts were twice-fold. You shouldn't say &quot;No&quot; to these kinds of effects but be prepared what your players can do with it. Having a mechanism in place to shut down the really game breaking stuff while leaving a space to actually cast the magic is key.<br /> <br /> Also, How DO You Do That, Masters of the Arts and other books clearly describe massive Paradox Backlashes happening due to Time related effects. It's imperative to note that while it is fun to use for all kind of shenanigans, the Time Sphere can and will destroy your game if not kept in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:22:45-08:00","id":1193672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1189153-can-mages-yank-something-from-the-past-or-future?p=1192537#post1192537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or what if the past changes because people share a wrong memory...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Czar Vargo? ;^)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}